{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLMS8x93ffdNiq1qNYUt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #252 as ready to plan: the triage engineer writes the plan and the engineer worker implements it. The routing file is at `.ard/252/triage-lead.md`.\n\nThe issue is a clear bug. If a reviewed pull request gets new code commits, the merger sees the review is out of date and refuses to merge. But nothing asks for the review again, so the pull request sits stuck until a person clears the review's done label. The fix belongs mainly in the merger and the review-coverage check (`internal/merger`, `internal/prgate`). It may also touch the reviewer's sweep that marks pull requests ready, and the merger section of the proposal doc needs updating.\n\n- **Planning:** only the engineer was requested. It's the only triage planner this repository has besides me. No architect or documentation planner exists to weigh in on the new event or the doc change, and I flagged that in the file's open issues.\n- **Review:** I added no review roles. The one reviewer, eng-review, has no `when:` rule in `.ard/config.yaml`, so it already runs on every pull request."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":623,"cache_read_input_tokens":11086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":623},"output_tokens":350,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"276c263d-cc3d-4a70-ba3c-958e79074603","uuid":"cfae5ca0-cb37-4b9c-b56f-32ca19ef4c41","timestamp":"2026-11-23T18:43:38.669Z","request_id":"req_011ChLMS8oxyRgPBAckkXsLA"}
